{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7b0e58428f53e3aaeaafb372","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1626","claim:pm-gh1630","claim:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-gh1630","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1626+pm-gh1630+pm-gh1633","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1626","claim:pm-gh1630","claim:pm-gh1633","lineage:pm-gh1630","lineage:pm-5t33or","lineage:pm-n7rr","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-covpax"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Successful linked-test receipts carry non-actionable execution_context and all-zero failure_categories, even under --lean"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while delivering pm-gh1630. After a selective run's tests[] was bounded to the selected entries, the remaining cost of a successful pm test --run receipt is mostly constant plumbing. On a 1-test --only-last run that passed: default TOON 2198 bytes, --lean 2178, --json 2685, --lean --json 2645. Every variant contains the full execution_context block (about 1.2 KB): requested and actual pm_context_mode, source and sandbox project and global paths, item counts, extension seeding flags, workspace roots and the trust fingerprint. It also contains a 9-row failure_categories map of zeros. When the run passed and mismatch_detected is false, an agent cannot act on any of it.\n\npm-fqdmbf (closed) hoisted the execution context to once per invocation and made --lean drop successful empty streams. Its acceptance criterion 'Lean structured output omits non-actionable successful-run sandbox plumbing while failures retain enough provenance' was delivered for streams only. This item covers the remaining boundary: what a successful, mismatch-free receipt must say about its sandbox, and whether all-zero failure categories need to be printed at all."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","linked-tests","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Measure the default, lean and JSON receipts for passing and failing runs, with and without a context mismatch; Define which execution_context fields are actionable on success and project the rest behind an explicit restore path, keeping full provenance on failure, refusal or mismatch; Render failure_categories compactly when every count is zero, without losing the counts on failure; Keep CLI, SDK and MCP shapes consistent and record the measured byte reduction"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A passing, mismatch-free linked-test receipt omits non-actionable sandbox plumbing and zero-count categories by default or under --lean, with a documented way to restore them; failures keep full diagnostic provenance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"cli"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-fqdmbf","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1630","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate check: a semantic search for execution_context and linked-test receipt verbosity, and a keyword search for execution_context. Closed pm-fqdmbf is the nearest owner. Its resolution records hoisting plus lean removal of successful streams only, and the live CLI shows execution_context in every variant, so this is a distinct, still-open boundary rather than a recurrence. Measured on this branch (feat/agent-same-command-corrections) in an isolated tracker."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"1dd67ca819fa3d429a66f957bf256791e0e1f81995611f38a283dc408355f9fa","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6c91963bf68c4d9282539390e4e586e44a32b81a09b4eac332f51e9d93cfb106"}
